# Findings Registry

<!-- The durable register of security and privacy findings for this project.

     One `##` block per finding, shaped per the plugin's reference/finding-contract.md:
     S-YYYYMMDD-NN id, status, check, disposition, severity/confidence/reachability,
     location, symptom, attack_path, concrete_input, blast_radius, root_cause_hypothesis,
     remediation, duplicate_of/ticket_link, first_seen/last_seen.

     NEW FINDINGS GO ABOVE THE `## Archive` HEADING. An entry below it is treated as
     resolved history and is invisible to the gate — appending to the end of this file is
     the natural mistake, so the gate blocks on any archived finding whose status is not
     `resolved` rather than trusting the placement.

     Deduplicate BY ROOT CAUSE, not by symptom text: four routes missing the same tenant
     scope because they bypass the same helper are ONE finding with four locations.

     This file is committable, and it is only safe to commit because of what it never
     contains — no credential value, no personal record, no working exploit. A finding names
     the location, the mechanism, and the fix. One that needs a payload to be understood is
     written wrong. See reference/safety.md.

     Resolved entries move to ## Archive. -->

